  "id": "trace-conditioning",
  "term": "trace conditioning",
  "definition": "Trace conditioning is a form of associative learning in which one stimulus is presented and the reinforcing stimulus comes later, separated by a time gap rather than overlapping. In the source example, an odor or visual cue is followed after a delay by shock, and the earlier cue is then linked to the later outcome.",
